      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would like to add a bit more about why I proposed the ear icon.\n\nAs of 1602, other players need to remember that \"audio is being sent to a distant location\". If there is an obstacle between them, a penetrating icon will intuitively convey the fact that it is being recorded.\n\nIn other words, this could be a video camera or microphone icon instead of an ear icon, and displaying a complex model and sound source instead of adding one in the instance would be a reduction in load. As an additional suggestion, XOR post-processing would be easier to remove in non-realtime cases.\n\nなぜ耳アイコンを提案したかについて補足します。\n\n1602 時点では、他のプレイヤーは「遠く離れた場所に音声が送信されている」ことを思い出す必要があります。もし間に障害物があっても、貫通的に表示されるアイコンであれば、直感的に収録の事実が伝わります。\n\n言い換えると、これは耳のアイコンではなくビデオカメラまたはマイクのアイコンでもかまわないし、複雑なモデルおよび音源をインスタンス内に１つ追加する代わりに表示することは負荷の低減になります。追加の提案として、非リアルタイムの場合は XOR 後処理を削除する方が簡単になります。",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-14T00:53:11.450Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Drones are a great filming tool, and the use of them could become popular, especially at events. I don't want to become a nuisance when i film events or fly around populated worlds. \n\nI understand that players can turn off drones and choose not to see them. As the pilot I feel like I should have the ability to turn off the drone model as well as being able to turn off the sound my drone makes for others.\n\nWhen the visibility of the drone is toggled off, the normal camera model should take it's place as to let people know they are on camera.",
